{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523307-learning-gift-alone","id":1523307,"title":"Learning gift Alone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-29T08:09:11-07:00","id":1523307,"title":"Learning gift Alone","content":"I'm wondering if a garou can, by any means, learn/develop gift without the intervention of spirits. A rites that enhance the Wyld part inside garou, a benediction from Ga\u00efa, a specific connection similar but deeper than the Spirit Heritage background, a place of power where it's possible through spiritual connection....<br /> <br /> I would like to create a special npc that is a source of secret my pc could meet and ask for favor, and if i give that pc that ability i would like to make it accurate with the lore. The way he would do it will not be given to the pc, obviously, this is only for story purpose","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T11:13:30-07:00","id":1523312,"title":"","content":"Garou can teach other Garou Gifts that they already know themselves. But of course those Garou most likely learned their Gifts from the spirits. And the spirits really dislike Garou sharing Gifts. We can assume that a promise to not teach any Gifts they learn is part of the normal chiminage a Garou gives the spirits when being taught, and it may even be a violation of the Pact. But it is one way you can avoid having the spirits teach a Garou directly. And there could be a Ronin Garou who was of relatively high rank and knew lots of Gifts before he committed the crimes that caused him to be banished. If he's in exile and bitter about Garou society, such an NPC could easily be a source to the PC (as well as any other Garou).<br /> <br /> If you want something more special, there are any number of unusual exemptions you could employ. You could decide one of the Kami can teach one or more Gifts to a Garou, though of course Kami are just spirits bonded to mortal humans, animals, plants, and animate lands. But they are very rare and always unique. The Book of the Wyld introduced the concept of &quot;Wyld fetishes&quot;, which aren't actual fetishes and not reproducible by Garou, but special blessings - often intended for a specific Garou. Because it is of the Wyld, you can use all sorts of strange and unique situations. It could be some kind of animal, plant, spring, or something else a Garou could consume and the result is that she suddenly knows a Gift she did not before. Or the Garou enters one of the Wyld Thresholds and the Threshold itself decides to impart a Gift to the Garou for whatever incomprehensible reasons of its own. I don't think &quot;teaching Gifts&quot; is associated with any of these concepts, but I don't see why you couldn't use them as a very unusual means of how it could happen. They are meant to be storytelling tools to allow the ST to do unusual things IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T12:37:36-07:00","id":1523317,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I didn't thougth about kami and wyld fetiche, they're indeed good solution. But i was meaning really alone, without needing anyone or anything to learn gifts.<br /> <br /> My first idea was that the npc i'm creating has somehow &quot;steal&quot; or &quot;assimilate&quot; a part of the wyld nature inside him during one of his journey in the Umbra. That fragment would allow gim to reproduce the spiritual nature of any kind of spirit and develop their gift without any help, but would suffer heavy counterpart to that (uncontrolable transformation, random frenezy, impossibility to concentrate, or something that make him a walking danger for the veil)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T13:18:30-07:00","id":1523322,"title":"","content":"Well a visit to a Flux Realm could certainly have that effect.<br /> <br /> Though I'm honestly not sure why you want to add all this complexity to it. The actually process of learning a Gift from a spirit is the quick and easy part. The books have long since established that there are secret Gifts you need to be taught about to know, and Gifts that the spirits will not teach if you're not a member of a specific group. The spirits can just say, &quot;we don't teach this Gift unless the current chosen person deems you worthy,&quot; and then you need to get the NPC to deem you worthy.<br /> <br /> If the players aren't really going to know the difference, I'm not sure why to make it so different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T15:18:23-07:00","id":1523327,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Honestly it's just because the lore is so fascinating that i need to know how it work in it's majority and what's possible or not to do, even if it's not useful or sure that my pc will ask for those detail or not x)<br /> I just like the world of darkness and it's possibility, so when i'm creating an npc and writting even a short story i like to add detail on him which are relevant to the lore or the universe logic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}